      "text_helper": "Section 43.7.34 \"LTDC layer x burst length configuration register (LTDC_LxBLCR)\" in chapter 43 (LCD-TFT display controller (LTDC)), RM0486 Rev 4, page 2140.",
      "section_content": "Address offset: 0x12C + 0x100 * (x - 1), (x = 1 to 2)\nReset value: 0x00000000\nThis register defines the length of the bursts requested by layer x.\nBits 31:5 Reserved, must be kept at reset value.\nBits 4:0 BL[4:0]: Burst length\nThis bitfield defines the burst length as number of 64-bit words.\n0x00: 16-word burst (maximum, 128 bytes)\n0x01: 1-word burst (8 bytes)\n0x02: 2-word burst (16 bytes)\n0x03: 3-word burst (24 bytes)\n0x04: 4-word burst (32 bytes)\n0x05: 5-word burst (40 bytes)\n0x06: 6-word burst (48 bytes)\n0x07: 7-word burst (56 bytes)\n0x08: 8-word burst (64 bytes)\n0x09: 9-word burst (72 bytes)\n0x0A: 10-word burst (80 bytes)\n0x0B: 11-word burst (88 bytes)\n0x0C: 12-word burst (96 bytes)\n0x0D: 13-word burst (104 bytes)\n0x0E: 14-word burst (112 bytes)\n0x0F: 15-word burst (120 bytes)\n0x10: 16-word burst (128 bytes)\nOther: Reserved",
